{"chunk_id": "Grapes_p0071_c0089", "doc_name": "Grapes.pdf", "doc_title": "AESA Based IPM Package - Grapes", "publisher": "DPPQS & NIPHM, Ministry of Agriculture, GoI", "year": 2014, "licence": "Government of India Public Domain", "page": 72, "language": "en", "crop_tags": ["general"], "disease_tags": ["general"], "has_dosage": false, "table_uncertain": false, "garbled": false, "no_text_layer": false, "text": "[disease comes from living tissues of host. Pruning] 72 natural enemies. 11. Diseases like downy mildew and powdery mildew are obligate parasites and active inoculum of disease comes from living tissues of host. Pruning of adjacent blocks if done keeping more than 9 days gap, pruned block provides inoculum on new growth emerged from pruned block. Hence time gap between two adjacent blocks should not be more than 9 days. If unavoidable, fungicide should be sprayed on un-pruned block . Col_0: 11. | Col_1: Diseases like downy mildew and powdery mildew are obligate parasites and active inoculum of disease comes from living tissues of host. Pruning of adjacent blocks if done keeping more than 9 days gap, pruned block provides inoculum on new growth emerged from pruned block. | natural enemies.: Hence time gap between two adjacent blocks should not be more than 9 days. If unavoidable, fungicide should be sprayed on un-pruned block .", "verbatim_text": "72 natural enemies. 11. Diseases like downy mildew and powdery mildew are obligate parasites and active inoculum of disease comes from living tissues of host. Pruning of adjacent blocks if done keeping more than 9 days gap, pruned block provides inoculum on new growth emerged from pruned block. Hence time gap between two adjacent blocks should not be more than 9 days. If unavoidable, fungicide should be sprayed on un-pruned block . Col_0: 11. | Col_1: Diseases like downy mildew and powdery mildew are obligate parasites and active inoculum of disease comes from living tissues of host. Pruning of adjacent blocks if done