{"chunk_id": "Maize_p0025_c0014", "doc_name": "Maize.pdf", "doc_title": "Integrated Pest Management Package for Maize", "publisher": "DPPQS & NCIPM, Ministry of Agriculture, GoI", "year": 2014, "licence": "Government of India Public Domain", "page": 26, "language": "en", "crop_tags": ["Corn"], "disease_tags": ["general"], "has_dosage": true, "table_uncertain": false, "garbled": false, "no_text_layer": false, "text": "[management.] 16 INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT PACKAGE FOR MAIZE Disease Resistant/tolerant varieties Brown Spot (Physoderma maydis Miyake) JH 10655, FH 3113 Banded Leaf and Sheath Blight (Rhizoctonia solani f. sp. sasakii Exner) PRATAP KANCHAN 2, PRATAP MAKKA 3, PRATAP MAKKA 5, SHAKTIMAN 1 and SHAKTIMAN 3 Pre-flowering Stalk Rots or Pythium Stalk Rot (Pythium aphanidermatum (Eds) Fitz) PEMH 1, X 1280 and HQPM 4 Bacterial Stalk Rot (Erwinia chrysanthemi p.v. zeae (Sabet) Victoria, Arboleda & Munoz.) PAU 352, PEMH 5, DKI 9202, DKI 9304 Post – flowering Stalk Rot ( Fusarium moniliforme Sheld.) PEMH 1, PEMH 2, PRATAP KANCHAN 2,PRATAP MAKKA 3, PRATAP MAKKA 5, SHEETAL, JH 6805, X 1280 Charcoal Rot (Macrophomina phaseolina (Goid) Tassi) JHMH 1701, JH 6805 and BIO 9639 Cyst nematode (Heterodera zeae Koshy et al.,) AGET-71 3.3.3 Mechanical Practices 1. Stripping of 2 lower leaves along with leaf sheath 2. Rogue and destroy infected plants & alternate host 3. Use bird scarer to prevent seed damage 3.3.4 Biological control 1. Add Trichoderma harzianum formulation 2.0% WP in furrows at the time of sowing prior mixing with FYM @ 10 g/kg FYM & incubated for 10 days in moist condition for Charcoal rot (Post flowering stalk rot) 2. Seed treatment with Trichoderma harzianum 2.0% WP @ 20 g/kg of seeds for control of Rhizoctonia solani f. sp. sasakii (Banded leaf & sheath blight) 3. Combined application of mustard & tobacco dust @ 2.5q/ha (ETL – 2 cyst/g of soil) for cyst nematode 4. Application of Trichogramma chilonis @ 1,60,000/ha. on 7 and 15 days old crop onwards at weekly interval for various pathogens. 3.3.5 Chemical control Need based and judicious application of fungicides are most important component of integrated pest management. 1. Seed treatment with Thiram 75% WS @ 25 to 30 g/kg seed. 2. Seed treatment with fungicide Metalaxyl-M 31.8% ES @ 2.4 ml/kg of seed in the endemic areas of downy mildews. 3.", "verbatim_text": "16 INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT PACKAGE FOR MAIZE Disease Resistant/tolerant varieties Brown Spot (Physoderma maydis Miyake) JH 10655, FH 3113 Banded Leaf and Sheath Blight (Rhizoctonia solani f. sp. sasakii Exner) PRATAP KANCHAN 2, PRATAP MAKKA 3, PRATAP MAKKA 5, SHAKTIMAN 1 and SHAKTIMAN 3 Pre-flowering Stalk Rots or Pythium Stalk Rot (Pythium aphanidermatum (Eds) Fitz) PEMH 1, X 1280 and HQPM 4 Bacterial Stalk Rot (Erwinia chrysanthemi p.v. zeae (Sabet) Victoria, Arboleda & Munoz.) PAU 352, PEMH 5, DKI 9202, DKI 9304 Post – flowering Stalk Rot ( Fusarium moniliforme Sheld.) PEMH 1, PEMH 2, PRATAP KANCHAN 2,PRATAP MAKKA 3, PRATAP MAKKA 5, SHEETAL, JH 6805, X 1280 Charcoal Rot (Macrophomina phaseolina (Goid) Tassi) JHMH 1701, JH 6805 and BIO 9639 Cyst nematode (Heterodera zeae Koshy et al.,) AGET-71 3.3.3 Mechanical Practices 1. Stripping of 2 lower leaves along with leaf sheath 2. Rogue and destroy infected plants & alternate host 3. Use bird scarer to prevent seed damage 3.3.4 Biological control 1. Add Trichoderma harzianum formulation 2.0% WP in furrows at the time of sowing prior mixing with FYM @ 10 g/kg FYM & incubated for 10 days in moist condition for Charcoal rot (Post flowering stalk rot) 2. Seed treatment with Trichoderma harzianum 2.0% WP @ 20 g/kg of seeds for control of Rhizoctonia solani f. sp. sasakii (Banded leaf & sheath blight) 3. Combined application of mustard & tobacco dust @ 2.5q/ha (ETL – 2 cyst/g of soil) for cyst nematode 4. Application of Trichogramma chilonis @ 1,60,000/ha. on 7 and 15 days old crop onwards at weekly interval for various pathogens. 3.3.5 Chemical control Need based and judicious application of fungicides are most important component of integrated pest management. 1. Seed treatment with Thiram 75% WS @ 25 to 30 g/kg seed. 2. Seed treatment with fungicide Metalaxyl-M 31.8% ES @ 2.4 ml/kg of seed in the endemic areas of downy mildews. 3.", "page_thumbnail_path": "kb\\pages\\Maize\\page_0025.png"}
