{"chunk_id": "Maize_p0029_c0025", "doc_name": "Maize.pdf", "doc_title": "Integrated Pest Management Package for Maize", "publisher": "DPPQS & NCIPM, Ministry of Agriculture, GoI", "year": 2014, "licence": "Government of India Public Domain", "page": 30, "language": "en", "crop_tags": ["Corn"], "disease_tags": ["general"], "has_dosage": true, "table_uncertain": false, "garbled": false, "no_text_layer": false, "text": "[Stage] 20 INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT PACKAGE FOR MAIZE Stage Name of pests Pests/Pathogens Practices Charcoal rot Macrophomina phaseolina (Goid) Tassi. 1. Sanitation and removal of previous crop debris 2. Deep ploughing 3. Avoiding water stress at flowering time reduces disease incidence 4. Balanced soil fertility, avoid high level of N and low level of K 5. Add Trichoderma harzianum formulation 2.0% WP in furrows at the time of sowing prior mixing with FYM @ 10 g/kg FYM & incubated for10 days in moist condition for Charcoal rot Late wilt Cephalosporium maydis Samara, Sabeti & Hingorani 1. Avoidance of moisture stress and balanced potash application reduce the incidence of the disease 2. Seed from infected areas should not be planted 3. Rotation with other crops Cyst nematode Heterodera zeae Koshy et al. 1. Deep summer ploughing 2-3 times at the interval of 10 to 15 days between April and May and summer fallowing with destruction of weeds 2. Use of non-cereal crops like vegetables, oilseeds and pulses etc., (When there are 3 cysts/g of soil) 3. Use of moderately resistant varieties like Ageti-71 4. Organic amendments like combined application of mustard cake and tobacco dust @ 2.5 q ha-1 5. Soil application of Carbofuran 3% CG @ 2.0 kg a.i ha-1 (4 cysts/g of soil) 6. Apply Neem cake @ 50 kg/ha. Name of pests: Charcoal rot | Pests/Pathogens: Macrophomina phaseolina (Goid) Tassi. | Practices: 1. Sanitation and removal of previous crop debris 2. Deep ploughing 3. Avoiding water stress at flowering time reduces disease incidence 4. Balanced soil fertility,