{"chunk_id": "Maize_p0040_c0034", "doc_name": "Maize.pdf", "doc_title": "Integrated Pest Management Package for Maize", "publisher": "DPPQS & NCIPM, Ministry of Agriculture, GoI", "year": 2014, "licence": "Government of India Public Domain", "page": 41, "language": "en", "crop_tags": ["Corn"], "disease_tags": ["general"], "has_dosage": false, "table_uncertain": false, "garbled": false, "no_text_layer": false, "text": "[INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT PACKAGE FOR MAIZE] 31 INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT PACKAGE FOR MAIZE Annexure-VII Operational, calibration and maintenance guidelines in brief S. No. Do’s Don’ts 1. For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide. 2. It is advisable to check the output of the sprayer (calibration) before commencement of spraying under guidance of trained person. 3. Clean and wash the machines and nozzles and store in dry place after use. 4. It is advisable to use protective clothing, face mask and gloves while preparing and applying pesticides. Do not apply pesticides without protective clothing and wash clothes immediately after spray application. 5. Do not apply in hot or windy conditions. 6. Operator should maintain normal walking speed while undertaking application. 7. Do not smoke, chew or eat while undertaking the spraying operation S. No.: 1. | Do’s: For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide. S. No.: 2. | Do’s: It is advisable to check the output of the sprayer (calibration) before commencement of spraying under guidance of trained person. S. No.: 3. | Do’s: Clean and wash the machines and nozzles and store in dry place after use. S. No.: 4. | Do’s: It is advisable to use protective clothing, face mask and gloves while preparing and applying pesticides. Do not apply pesticides without protective clothing and wash clothes immediately after spray application. S. No.: 5. | Do’s: Do not apply in hot or windy conditions. S. No.: 6. | Do’s: Operator should maintain normal walking speed while undertaking application. S. No.: 7. | Do’s: Do not smoke, chew or eat while undertaking the spraying operation Col_0: 31", "verbatim_text": "31 INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT PACKAGE FOR MAIZE Annexure-VII Operational, calibration and maintenance guidelines in brief S. No. Do’s Don’ts 1. For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide. 2. It is advisable to check the output of the sprayer (calibration) before commencement of spraying under guidance of trained person. 3. Clean and wash the machines and nozzles and store in dry place after use. 4. It is advisable to use protective clothing, face mask and gloves while preparing and applying pesticides. Do not apply pesticides without protective clothing and wash clothes immediately after spray application. 5. Do not apply in hot or windy conditions. 6. Operator should maintain normal walking speed while undertaking application. 7. Do not smoke, chew or eat while undertaking the spraying operation S. No.: 1. | Do’s: For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide. S. No.: 2. | Do’s: It is advisable to check the output of the sprayer (calibration) before commencement of spraying under guidance of trained person. S. No.: 3. | Do’s: Clean and wash the machines and nozzles and store in dry place after use. S. No.: 4. | Do’s: It is advisable to use protective clothing, face mask and gloves while preparing and applying pesticides. Do not apply pesticides without protective clothing and wash clothes immediately after spray application. S. No.: 5. | Do’s: Do not apply in hot or windy conditions. S. No.: 6. | Do’s: Operator should maintain normal walking speed while undertaking application. S. No.: 7. | Do’s: Do not smoke, chew or eat while undertaking the spraying operation Col_0: 31", "page_thumbnail_path": "kb\\pages\\Maize\\page_0040.png"}
