{"chunk_id": "Potato_p0069_c0079", "doc_name": "Potato.pdf", "doc_title": "AESA Based IPM Package - Potato", "publisher": "DPPQS & NIPHM, Ministry of Agriculture, GoI", "year": 2014, "licence": "Government of India Public Domain", "page": 70, "language": "en", "crop_tags": ["Potato"], "disease_tags": ["general"], "has_dosage": false, "table_uncertain": false, "garbled": false, "no_text_layer": false, "text": "[XVI. OPERATIONAL, CALIBRATION AND MAINTENANCE GUIDELINES IN BRIEF] 58 AESA based IPM – Potato XVI. OPERATIONAL, CALIBRATION AND MAINTENANCE GUIDELINES IN BRIEF 1. For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide. 2. It is advisable to check the output of the sprayer (calibration) before commencement of spraying under guidance of trained person. 3. Clean and wash the machines and nozzles and store in dry place after use. 4. It is advisable to use protective clothing, face mask and gloves while preparing and applying pesticides. Do not apply pesticides without protective clothing and wash clothes immediately after spray application. 5. Do not apply in hot or windy conditions. 6. Operator should maintain normal walking speed while undertaking application. 7. Do not smoke, chew or eat while undertaking the spraying operation 8. Operator should take proper bath with soap after completing spraying 9. Do not blow the nozzle with mouth for any blockages. Clean with water and a soft brush. 1.: 2. | For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide.: It is advisable to check the output of the sprayer (calibration) before commencement of spraying under guidance of trained person. 1.: 3. | For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide.: Clean and wash the machines and nozzles and store in dry place after use. 1.: 4. | For application rate and dosage see the label and leaflet of the particular pesticide.: It is advisable to use protective clothing, face mask and